    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11300" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπαλλ-ακτικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fit for ridding, removing,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρόφων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dsc.
					3.72
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νοσήματος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					1.345
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>fit for curing illness,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				959b26
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς, ἔχειν,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπαλλαξείειν</span>
			, <i>wish to depart,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				11.8
			</span></i>.</div>
